Dear Reviewer,

&nbsp;

First, we want to thank you for appreciating the new theoretical analysis and for confirming that it addresses one of your concerns.

&nbsp;

Regarding the concern raised by other reviewers about the effectiveness of our method (JCB) under the Self Reminder defense: In our original response, we only reported results in the **non-adaptive setting** (i.e., where the attacker is unaware of the defense) due to resource constraints and the need to prioritize other major experiments (e.g., ablations, theoretical analysis, and broader baseline comparisons). Under that setting, as noted previously, JCB does not bypass Self Reminder.

&nbsp;

However, since this point is causing the reviewer to question JCB’s overall efficacy, we have now conducted new experiments in an **adaptive setting**, where the attacker is aware of the deployed defense. In this setting, JCB successfully circumvents the Self Reminder defense by simply incorporating instructions to ignore Self Reminder’s system prompt and incorporating it within JCB. Across all tested models, JCB achieves high adaptive ASR, as shown below and included in the revised manuscript (Table 15, Appendix O):

&nbsp;

| Models | GPT-3.5 Turbo 1106 | GPT-4o 2024-05-13 | GPT-4o-mini | Llama 3.1 405B | Avg.  |
|----------------------|--------------------|-------------------|-------------|-----------------|-------|
| JCB ASR          | 100                 | 100                | 98          | 100              | 99.5  |

&nbsp;

In summary, we believe our original response addressed your concerns about the semantic coherence of our attack prompts, investigation into the underlying mechanisms, and ablation studies. Additionally, we hope these new results fully address your concern about the effectiveness of our attack under the Self Reminder defense. We hope you will reconsider updating your score given the new evidence we presented above.

&nbsp;

Finally, we genuinely appreciate your feedback. It has really helped improve our work. If you have any additional concerns, we would be more than happy to address them.
